From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test_sshkey: pass the_banana array, not banana function, to memcpy

test_sshkey.c's banana() helper copies the const u_char the_banana[]
array across buffer s in chunks, but line 143 passes the function
pointer banana (not the array) as memcpy's 2nd arg:

  memcpy(s + o, banana, sizeof(the_banana));

clang rejects assigning a function pointer to const void *:

  error: no matching function for call to 'memcpy'
  note: candidate function not viable: no known conversion from
        'void (u_char *, size_t)' to 'const void *' for 2nd argument

7.5p1 through 7.9p1 all carry this typo; older gccs accepted it.
Fix the one token so the test compiles on OHOS's clang toolchain.

---
 regress/unittests/sshkey/test_sshkey.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/regress/unittests/sshkey/test_sshkey.c b/regress/unittests/sshkey/test_sshkey.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/regress/unittests/sshkey/test_sshkey.c
+++ b/regress/unittests/sshkey/test_sshkey.c
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ banana(u_char *s, size_t l)
 		if (l - o < sizeof(the_banana)) {
 			memcpy(s + o, "nanananana", l - o);
 			break;
 		}
-		memcpy(s + o, banana, sizeof(the_banana));
+		memcpy(s + o, the_banana, sizeof(the_banana));
 	}
 }

--
